-- title:
--   Theorem 4.3 — all four equivalent clauses of the complex Nullstellensatz
-- statement:
--   Let $f_1,\ldots,f_s\in\mathbb C[x_1,\ldots,x_n]$, and let $I=\langle f_1,\ldots,f_s\rangle$. All four assertions of Hilbert's Nullstellensatz in Theorem 4.3 are equivalent:
--   $$\{x\in\mathbb C^n:\forall i,\ f_i(x)=0\}=\varnothing\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad1\in I\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad I=\mathbb C[x_1,\ldots,x_n]\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad\exists g_1,\ldots,g_s,\ \sum_i f_i g_i=1.$$
--   This is the entire finite-family theorem over the complex numbers, including necessity and the explicit certificate. It is a companion theorem; the published goal is left unchanged.
--
--   **Formalization Note** `List.TFAE` expresses equivalence of all four propositions. The generated ideal is `Ideal.span (Set.range f)` and the whole ring is the top ideal. Polynomial identities are equalities of multivariate polynomials, so (4.2) holds identically. The variable count and number of equations may be zero; the empty common-zero condition and empty certificate sum have their usual meanings.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: four statements are equivalent → List.TFAE of the four source propositions; reason: preserves all clauses and both directions.
--   - encoding: the ideal generated by f₁,…,fₛ → Ideal.span (Set.range f); reason: the generated ideal is the finite polynomial-multiplier ideal of Definition 4.2.
-- source:
--   Parrilo, Semidefinite programming relaxations for semialgebraic problems, Math. Program. Ser. B 96 (2003) 293–320, p. 302–303, Theorem 4.3 (Hilbert’s Nullstellensatz)

import Mathlib

namespace SemialgebraicSDP.Copositive.Supplement

/-- All four equivalent clauses of Theorem 4.3 (pp. 302–303), over ℂ. -/
theorem theorem_4_3 {n s : ℕ} (f : Fin s → MvPolynomial (Fin n) ℂ) :
    List.TFAE [
      {x : Fin n → ℂ | ∀ i, MvPolynomial.eval x (f i) = 0} = ∅,
      (1 : MvPolynomial (Fin n) ℂ) ∈ Ideal.span (Set.range f),
      Ideal.span (Set.range f) = ⊤,
      ∃ g : Fin s → MvPolynomial (Fin n) ℂ, ∑ i, f i * g i = 1] := by sorry

end SemialgebraicSDP.Copositive.Supplement
